166:     /**
167:      * Different from {@link #requestUnpooledMemorySegments} for unpooled segments allocation. This
168:      * method and the below {@link #requestPooledMemorySegmentsBlocking} method are designed to be
169:      * used from {@link LocalBufferPool} for pooled memory segments allocation. Note that these
170:      * methods for pooled memory segments requesting and recycling are prohibited from acquiring the
171:      * factoryLock to avoid deadlock.
172:      */
173:     @Nullable
174:     public MemorySegment requestPooledMemorySegment() {
175:         synchronized (availableMemorySegments) {
