682:     /**
683:      * Sets the state backend that describes how to store operator. It defines the data structures
684:      * that hold state during execution (for example hash tables, RocksDB, or other data stores).
685:      *
686:      * <p>State managed by the state backend includes both keyed state that is accessible on {@link
687:      * org.apache.flink.streaming.api.datastream.KeyedStream keyed streams}, as well as state
688:      * maintained directly by the user code that implements {@link
689:      * org.apache.flink.streaming.api.checkpoint.CheckpointedFunction CheckpointedFunction}.
690:      *
691:      * <p>The {@link org.apache.flink.runtime.state.hashmap.HashMapStateBackend} maintains state in
692:      * heap memory, as objects. It is lightweight without extra dependencies, but is limited to JVM
693:      * heap memory.
694:      *
695:      * <p>In contrast, the {@code EmbeddedRocksDBStateBackend} stores its state in an embedded
696:      * {@code RocksDB} instance. This state backend can store very large state that exceeds memory
697:      * and spills to local disk. All key/value state (including windows) is stored in the key/value
698:      * index of RocksDB.
699:      *
700:      * <p>In both cases, fault tolerance is managed via the jobs {@link
701:      * org.apache.flink.runtime.state.CheckpointStorage} which configures how and where state
702:      * backends persist during a checkpoint.
703:      *
704:      * @deprecated The method is marked as deprecated because starting from Flink 1.19, the usage of
705:      *     all complex Java objects related to configuration, including their getter and setter
706:      *     methods, should be replaced by ConfigOption. In a future major version of Flink, this
707:      *     method will be removed entirely. It is recommended to switch to using the ConfigOptions
708:      *     provided for configuring state backend like the following code snippet:
709:      *     <pre>{@code
710:      * Configuration config = new Configuration();
711:      * config.set(StateBackendOptions.STATE_BACKEND, "hashmap");
