746:     /**
747:      * Enable the change log for current state backend. This change log allows operators to persist
748:      * state changes in a very fine-grained manner. Currently, the change log only applies to keyed
749:      * state, so non-keyed operator state and channel state are persisted as usual. The 'state' here
750:      * refers to 'keyed state'. Details are as follows:
751:      *
752:      * <p>Stateful operators write the state changes to that log (logging the state), in addition to
753:      * applying them to the state tables in RocksDB or the in-mem Hashtable.
754:      *
755:      * <p>An operator can acknowledge a checkpoint as soon as the changes in the log have reached
756:      * the durable checkpoint storage.
757:      *
758:      * <p>The state tables are persisted periodically, independent of the checkpoints. We call this
759:      * the materialization of the state on the checkpoint storage.
760:      *
761:      * <p>Once the state is materialized on checkpoint storage, the state changelog can be truncated
762:      * to the corresponding point.
763:      *
764:      * <p>It establish a way to drastically reduce the checkpoint interval for streaming
765:      * applications across state backends. For more details please check the FLIP-158.
766:      *
767:      * <p>If this method is not called explicitly, it means no preference for enabling the change
768:      * log. Configs for change log enabling will override in different config levels
769:      * (job/local/cluster).
