856:     /**
857:      * Assigns timestamps to the elements in the data stream and generates watermarks to signal
858:      * event time progress. The given {@link WatermarkStrategy} is used to create a {@link
859:      * TimestampAssigner} and {@link WatermarkGenerator}.
860:      *
861:      * <p>For each element in the data stream, the {@link TimestampAssigner#extractTimestamp(Object,
862:      * long)} method is called to assign an event timestamp.
863:      *
864:      * <p>For each event in the data stream, the {@link WatermarkGenerator#onEvent(Object, long,
865:      * WatermarkOutput)} will be called.
866:      *
867:      * <p>Periodically (defined by the {@link ExecutionConfig#getAutoWatermarkInterval()}), the
868:      * {@link WatermarkGenerator#onPeriodicEmit(WatermarkOutput)} method will be called.
869:      *
870:      * <p>Common watermark generation patterns can be found as static methods in the {@link
871:      * org.apache.flink.api.common.eventtime.WatermarkStrategy} class.
872:      *
873:      * @param watermarkStrategy The strategy to generate watermarks based on event timestamps.
874:      * @return The stream after the transformation, with assigned timestamps and watermarks.
875:      */
876:     public SingleOutputStreamOperator<T> assignTimestampsAndWatermarks(
877:             WatermarkStrategy<T> watermarkStrategy) {
878:         final WatermarkStrategy<T> cleanedStrategy = clean(watermarkStrategy);
879:         // match parallelism to input, to have a 1:1 source -> timestamps/watermarks relationship
880:         // and chain
881:         final int inputParallelism = getTransformation().getParallelism();
882:         final TimestampsAndWatermarksTransformation<T> transformation =
883:                 new TimestampsAndWatermarksTransformation<>(
884:                         "Timestamps/Watermarks",
885:                         inputParallelism,
886:                         getTransformation(),
887:                         cleanedStrategy,
