46: /**
47:  * This class encapsulates state handles to the snapshots of all operator instances executed within
48:  * one task. A task can run multiple operator instances as a result of operator chaining, and all
49:  * operator instances from the chain can register their state under their operator id. Each operator
50:  * instance is a physical execution responsible for processing a partition of the data that goes
51:  * through a logical operator. This partitioning happens to parallelize execution of logical
52:  * operators, e.g. distributing a map function.
53:  *
54:  * <p>One instance of this class contains the information that one task will send to acknowledge a
55:  * checkpoint request by the checkpoint coordinator. Tasks run operator instances in parallel, so
56:  * the union of all {@link TaskStateSnapshot} that are collected by the checkpoint coordinator from
57:  * all tasks represent the whole state of a job at the time of the checkpoint.
58:  *
